Meaning of the word

Saha—He, Balaramji; Bhima-Duryodhanaayoha—between Bhima and Duryodhana; Gadabhyam—with maces; Yudhyatoaha—while fighting;
Mridhe—in the battlefield; Vaarayishyan—wanting to refuse; Vinashanam—up to the battlefield; Jagam—went; Yadu—of the Yadus;
Nandanaha—beloved son (Balarama). At that time, with the desire to stop the mace fight going on between Bhima and Duryodhana in the battlefield,
Balramji went to Kurukshetra. Yudhishthira, seeing that, even Krishna and Arjuna... The abhivyakti (expression) is not something to be asked for here. 2. Meaning of the word

Yudhishthira - King Yudhishthira; Tu - but; Tam - him, Balarama; Drishtva - seeing; Yamau - twin brothers, Nakula and Sahadeva;
Krishna-Arjunaau - Krishna and Arjuna; Api - also; Abhivadya - saluting; Abhavan - had; Tushnim - silence; Kim - what;
Vivakshu - wanting to say; Iha - here; Agatah - has come.
When Yudhishthira, Krishna, Arjuna, and the twin brothers Nakula and Sahadeva saw Balram,
they all greeted him, but thinking, "What have they come to tell us?" they
remained silent. Meaning: Srila Prabhupada writes, "The reason for their silence was that Balaramji was somewhat affectionate towards Duryodhana,
because he had learned the art of mace fighting from him." Therefore, when the war was going on, King Yudhishthira and others thought that it was possible that Balramji might have come to say something in favor of Duryodhana. That is why he remained silent."

Gadapani, seeing the two, the victorious ones. The assembled ones, moving in a variety of ways, spoke. 25. Meaning of the words.

Gada—maces; Pani—held in hand; Ubhau—both of them, Duryodhana and Bhima; Drishtva—by seeing; Sarrbhadau—angry; Vijay—win;
Eshinau—efforting for; Mandalani—cycle, sphere; Vichitrani—artistic; Charantau—wandering; Idam—this;
Abraveet—said.
Balram saw that Duryodhana and Bhima, holding maces in their hands, were artistically
spinning and trying to gain victory over each other, filled with anger. God addressed them
in this way.

