Meaning: After praising the sense of hearing dedicated to God in the previous verse, King
Parikshit also mentions the other senses, so that we can get a complete picture of Krishna consciousness.
May it be possible. Here, they explain that all the parts of the body become useless if their connection is not with Krishna.
It remains. In the third chapter of the second book, in verses 20 to 2, Shaunak Rishi has given a similar statement.
It has been given. Srila Vishwanath Chakravarti mentions that in Krishna consciousness, all the senses should work together. In other words, whatever the eyes or ears may experience, the mind should only remember the omnipresent Krishna. He who has both arms and legs,
He who sees that, beholds it with his eyes.
Those who worship the feet of Vishnu,
They who worship the water of the feet, daily. Meaning of the word

Shirah - head; Tu-Tatha; Tasya - his; Ubhaya - both; Lingam - for expression; Anamet - bows; Tat - that;
Eva - only; Yat - which; Pashyati - sees; Tat - that; Hi - without doubt; Chakshuh - eye; Angani - limbs; Vishnouh - of Vishnu; Ath - or; Tat - his; Jananam - of the devotees; Pad-Udakam - water obtained by washing the feet; Yani - which;
Bhajanti - worship; Nityam - regularly;
Chakshuh - eye; Angani - limbs; Vishnouh - of Vishnu; Ath - or; Tat - his; Jananam - of the devotees; Pad-Udakam - water obtained by washing the feet; Yani - which;
Bhajanti - worship; Nityam - regularly;
Chakshuh - eye; Angani - limbs;.

The real head is the one that bows to the expressions of God between the inert and the conscious. The real eyes are those that witness only God, and the real limbs are those that
regularly respect the water obtained by washing the feet of God or his devotees.
They do. Suta said:
Vishnurate's request was fulfilled by the Lord's servant.
Vasudeva, the divine, spoke with a heart immersed in devotion. 5. Meaning of the word.

Soota said—Soot Goswami said; Vishnu-Raten—by Vishnu Rat (Maharaj Parikshit); Samprishtah—asked well;
Bhagavant—powerful sage; Badarayanih—Shukdev; Vasudeva—in Vasudeva; Bhagavati—God; Nimagna—completely immersed;
Hridayah—those with hearts; Abraveet—spoke.
